  "The problem with a number",
  "The product has exactly one organising principle: a document is a conversion of the document before it, and every number on it keeps the context it was calculated with. Everything else — the wizard, the engine, the delivery chain — follows from that.",
  "The product's own vocabulary",
  "The proforma is priced by specification group: clear tempered for the main facade, tinted where the sun hits, and a double-glazed Low-E unit for the energy-efficient zones. Each line carries its specification exactly as Step 5 holds it — serial, glass reference, outer pane W1 × H1, inner pane W2 × H2 where there is one, quantity, area, rate and value.",
  "The ProGlass Automation interface: dashboards, the proforma wizard, glass calculators, the optimization workspace, sheet store, delivery and reports.",
  "The ProGlass workflow stage by stage: inquiry, the 9-step proforma wizard, job order, production stages, multi-movement delivery, VAT invoices and statements.",
  "The project's history is written down, dated, and open to reading.",
  "The quotation",
  "The quote is not a document, it is a calculation",
  "The rack, as records: buy and use movements with history, never an edited number.",
